ments.\n\n- The statement “$f(x)$ has a critical point at $x=-1$” is true. The function has a critical point (a corner) at $x=-1.$ In this case,  ${f}^{′}(-1)$ does not exist.\n\n- The statement “$f(x)$ has a stationary point at $x=1$” is false. The function has a critical point (a corner) at $x=1.$ In this case,  ${f}^{′}(-1)$ does not exist.\n\n- The statement “$f(x)$ has a local maximum at $x=3$” is false. The function has a local minimum at $x=3$ since $f(3)\\le f(x)$ for all $x$ close enough to $x=3.$\n\nTherefore, select only “$f(x)$ has a critical point at $x=-1$.”"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329838 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b5ea4a7-acc4-5825-b6c5-b6c87e6a1674" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Critical and Stationary Points of a Function Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "652e1d3c-ce79-571d-becc-9c00c37f4c74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186730145} {:answer/id #uuid "8d872554-97ae-54c1-9f4e-c7d750586d30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186730146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "652e1d3c-ce79-571d-becc-9c00c37f4c74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186730145} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e826697-d1ad-5455-bf98-b59520e6b053" :answer-field/key "$x=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186730202} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24e40deb-9f16-52bc-a416-a84ae7f57aea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186730147} {:answer/id #uuid "7594def0-6497-58ef-932a-0ba92a5bad25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186730148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7594def0-6497-58ef-932a-0ba92a5bad25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type