18116bd2daa07f1375a3fb277c47ec8503fec90da824cd714d0b.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is plotted above. Given that $f(x)$ is defined on the interval $x\\in [-2,10],$ which points represent the global maximum of $f(x)$ ?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The global extrema of a function are the lowest or highest points of the function's graph over its entire domain.\n\nThe lowest point is the global minimum, whereas the highest point is the global maximum.\n\nAccording to the graph, the highest point is $D,$ and so this point represents the global maximum of $f(x).$ \n\n**Note:** The point $B$ is not a global maximum, it's a local maximum."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402909 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064162 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a595bc07-ad64-537d-be42-06144814b97d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Extrema of a Function Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1bb4bbb-2f02-50e1-b55d-7e77f3b78b12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473162} {:answer/id #uuid "c6ed7761-00f8-51d4-8735-0e72b6326883" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473163}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1bb4bbb-2f02-50e1-b55d-7e77f3b78b12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473162} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee30d273-5240-5e4c-a488-eda4ce0e214b" :answer-field/key "Point $A$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473976} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e39929d-71c5-5ec4-9835-ad2e78bc6b89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473164} {:answer/id #uuid "9047721c-4c2b-5ea1-a4ce-8f02ff331134" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9047721c